Subject: fixes register value aliasing, iterator close and two reference leaks

What this does
  Makes every part of the register compiler agree on which stack values are
  aliases, keeps for-await loops closable, and stops two handlers leaking a
  reference.

Why we need it
  The stack-shaper alias change left `nip` without a value definition and left
  the slot-forwarding model naming shaper outputs as fresh values, so logical
  assignment and `yield*` results read stale registers. The for-await step's
  `dup3; drop` then removed the loop's iterator record, so an exception no longer
  closed the iterator. `define_global_func` and `define_method` duplicated values
  their callees only borrow, leaking one reference per call.

What it adds
  `nip` in the shaper alias table, alias-aware slot forwarding, a sentinel drop
  only on the last stack reference, and borrowing calls to
  JS_DefineGlobalFunction and JS_DefineProperty.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No. The emitted register bytecode for the built-in blobs is unchanged.

